 "capsule": "The Southern Song (南宋, 1127–1279) was formed when the Song imperial clan fled south after Jurchen Jin forces captured the Northern Song capital Kaifeng and took Emperor Qinzong prisoner in the Jingkang Incident. Zhao Gou (Emperor Gaozong) reestablished the dynasty at Lin'an (modern Hangzhou), presiding over an era of commercial dynamism, maritime trade, and technological innovation even as the state paid tribute to the Jin. The Southern Song was the last major East Asian power to fall to the Mongols, surrendering after the naval defeat at Yamen in 1279.",
